Third-party dependencies

The Assay library itself has one dependency:

  swift-syntax — https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-syntax
  Copyright (c) Apple Inc. and the Swift project authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 with Runtime Library Exception
  See https://swift.org/LICENSE.txt

It is a build-time dependency of the AssayMacros plugin. It is not linked into a
client binary, and no other package is depended on by any shipped product.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

yyjson (https://github.com/ibireme/yyjson)
  Copyright (c) 2020 YaoYuan
  Licensed under the MIT License

Vendored at Benchmarks/Sources/CYYJSON as a BENCHMARK BASELINE only. It is not a
dependency of any shipped product, is not linked into a client binary, and no
Assay source file imports it. It exists so the comparison against a SIMD-tier C
parser in Benchmarks/RESULTS.md can be reproduced.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Benchmark-only package dependencies

These are SwiftPM dependencies of Benchmarks/Package.swift, which is a separate
package. They are not dependencies of any shipped product, are not linked into a
client binary, and no Assay source file imports them. They exist as ORACLES and
BASELINES so the numbers in Benchmarks/RESULTS.md can be reproduced.

  Yams (https://github.com/jpsim/Yams)
    Copyright (c) 2016 JP Simard
    Licensed under the MIT License
    Wraps libyaml. The differential oracle for Assay's YAML parser, and the
    baseline for the YAML rows.

  ZippyJSON (https://github.com/michaeleisel/ZippyJSON)
    Copyright (c) 2019 Michael Eisel
    Licensed under the MIT License
    simdjson wired to Decodable. The decoder Assay's falsification condition is
    stated against; see Benchmarks/RESULTS.md. Brings transitive dependencies on
    ZippyJSONCFamily and JJLISO8601DateFormatter, also MIT, likewise
    benchmark-only.
